Butterscotch ice cream is rare, I now know why it is. It's not difficult to make but people panic when the "Butter" goes anywhere which is a shame as this ice cream has the potential to be  BEAUTIFUL and is (if only for 2 days!).

EDIT: ON DAY 3 IN THE FREEZER , THE HIGH BUTTERFAT BECOMES VERY NOTICABLE. I'M GOING TO MAKE THIS AGAIN IN A FEW WEEKS WHICH WILL SORT THIS ISSUE BUT IF YOU WANT IT, THE RECIPE IS BELOW.

What you need:

Honeycomb Candy/Hokey Pokey/Cinder Toffee:
200g sugar
100g golden syrup/corn syrup
10g Bicarbonate of soda

Ice Cream Base: (this will all change in the next version of this ice cream)
350ml Milk @ 2% 
350ml Cream @ 33% 
80g Brown Sugar
10g Dextrose
2 Egg yolks
90g of Butterscotch Sauce (see below) keep the rest (heat to 107c MAX)
55g SMP
1.5g Stabiliser (or 2 egg yolks) 

Butterscotch Sauce: 
150g Brown Sugar
90g Butter
90g Cream

Yes there a few components, you don't need to make all of it, the honeycomb candy is a luxury add in for this recipe. 

